 by `regver`, not `impact_model_version`; decide.py comments cite 'calibration 3' moving the lowest threshold to 0.60","AC1 segments identity only 'for reviews whose impact_model_version matches current' — it does not segment on registry/regver"],"finding":"The baseline replay re-resolves per-criterion thresholds live from the criteria registry (via orchestrator.pass3_over_findings -> registry.by_id()), but the stored decision was judged against the per-finding block_threshold/blocking_enabled persisted losslessly in the v2 sidecar. Since thresholds live in criteria_routing.json (governed by `regver`) — a version axis DISTINCT from impact_model_version, which is all AC1 segments on — any registry threshold recalibration since a review ran will make `--candidate current` flip verdicts against the stored decision even when impact_model_version matches, so AC1's 'zero verdict flips' can fail for reasons unrelated to a harness bug.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f10e63471af1a00b8","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context (\"byte-identical to production\") + AC1","norm_id":"n7dc64b71aef5231c","priority":0.8,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A criterion's block_threshold or default_posture changed in criteria_routing.json after some corpus reviews were signed; those reviews still have current impact_model_version but their live-resolved threshold now differs from the persisted one, flipping block<->advisory in the baseline and failing AC1"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"For the AC1 identity check, feed pass3_decide the persisted per-finding block_threshold/blocking_enabled (a truly byte-identical replay of the stored decision), OR additionally segment/skip reviews whose signed regver differs from current and state that in the report; reserve the live-registry resolution for the candidate/what-if path.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the exact computation of 'friction rate' (numerator, denominator, and the population of reviews/findings it aggregates over) in the plan.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.064,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Approach: 'three-way verdict flip matrix, friction rate, per-criterion block/advisory/drop deltas, priority distribution shift'","AC3: 'The report contains a three-way verdict flip matrix, friction rate, and per-criterion deltas'","No formula given for 'friction rate' — a derived metric with no computation protocol is an ordinary E2 data-design ambiguity"],"finding":"'Friction rate' is named as a required report metric (Approach and AC3) but its computation/aggregation protocol is never stated — what numerator/denominator over which reviews defines it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f95968e8815e2a317","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach 'Report (...): ... friction rate ...'; AC3","norm_id":"n558d0389712c0976","priority":0.536,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Two implementers compute 'friction rate' differently (e.g. share of findings that flip block->advisory vs share of reviews with any flip), producing incomparable reports"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add a one-line definition, e.g. 'friction rate = fraction of findings whose candidate verdict is stricter (advisory->block or drop->advisory) than baseline, over all replayed findings.'","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Define the 'noise band' used in AC4 (its value/source — e.g. derived from labels.py inter-rater variance or a fixed tolerance) so the label-proxy annotation is buildable and verifiable.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2","F1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.131,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC4: 'label-proxy metrics with coverage fraction, annotated against the noise band'","No definition of 'noise band' (a threshold/derived value) appears in Context, Approach, or elsewhere — a derived metric with no stated source is an E2 signal (1)/(2) ambiguity","AC4 is only checkable 'when available', but even then 'annotated against the noise band' cannot be evaluated without the band's provenance"],"finding":"The 'noise band' referenced in AC4 ('label-proxy metrics with coverage fraction, annotated against the noise band') is never defined anywhere in the plan — no value, source, or computation is given, so the annotation is neither buildable nor verifiable.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbcb7a6db32799b53","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, AC4; Approach 'label-proxy metrics with coverage fraction'","norm_id":"nfe58d626c9076746","priority":0.469,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor builds the label-proxy annotation and must invent a noise-band value, or the reviewer of AC4 cannot confirm the annotation is correct"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"State where the noise band comes from (e.g. 'the label agreement band documented in docs/calibration/...' or an explicit ± tolerance) and how the label-proxy metric is compared against it.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Either extract orchestrator._threshold_for into a shared, registry-parameterized helper both production and the candidate path call, OR add a test that pins the mirrored candidate threshold logic (special-case + execution_review bump branches) byte-identical to production's closure under a non-empty overlay, so the two cannot drift.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["orchestrator.pass3_over_findings (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/orchestrator.py:681-689) defines _threshold_for as a closure: `if \"prerequisite-consistency\" in set(criteria): return 0.60, True` else `_criteria.threshold_for(criteria, crit_by_id, gate=\"plan_review\")` then `if execution_review and blocking_enabled: block_threshold = max(block_threshold, 0.80)`","Plan: 'The candidate path MIRRORS _threshold_for's exact logic (same special case, same bump, same veto restriction)'","The identity test only pins the EMPTY-overlay ('current') mirror against production; the special-case and execution_review-bump branches under a non-empty overlay are exercised in the mirror but not cross-checked against production's closure"],"finding":"The candidate path reimplements production's _threshold_for logic (special case, execution_review bump, veto restriction) rather than extracting/sharing the existing closure, creating a drift-prone duplicate of shipped decision logic.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff8a3a4816db68e8d","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section, 'Candidate' bullet; and Context paragraph 'A CANDIDATE overlay...MIRRORS _threshold_for's exact logic'","norm_id":"n61f6d3373df7dfc9","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future edit to production's _threshold_for (e.g. changing the 0.60 prerequisite-consistency threshold or the 0.80 execution bump) silently diverges from the mirrored candidate copy, so candidate replays are scored against stale posture logic while claiming byte-parity with production"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Refactor _threshold_for out of the pass3_over_findings closure into a module-level function taking (criteria, crit_by_id, execution_review) so both the production wrapper and the candidate path invoke the SAME implementation against their respective (baseline vs overlay-merged) registries — eliminating the duplicate.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impac